# CODEOWNERS — coverage model (un-inverted).
#
# DEFAULT = UNOWNED: any path not matched below needs no code-owner review, so a
# low-risk deterministic PR (and a Margot LOW-risk verdict) can merge without the
# operator. There is deliberately NO `* @owner` catch-all.
#
# OWNED (listed below) = paths where a JUDGMENT change must have a human: the
# safety / identity / gate machinery. The branch ruleset requires code-owner
# review (with 0 baseline approvals), so touching any owned path holds the PR for
# @lexijamesesq; touching only unowned paths does not.
#
# When adding a path: uncertain -> OWNED (under-coverage — an owned path left
# unowned — is the dangerous direction).

# --- Gate machinery (CI + release) ---
/.github/workflows/                             @lexijamesesq
/.github/dependabot.yml                         @lexijamesesq

# --- Gate / lint configs (can DISABLE a check) ---
/.pre-commit-config.yaml                        @lexijamesesq
/.gitleaks.toml                                 @lexijamesesq
/.gitleaks-ci.toml                              @lexijamesesq
/.house-code.json                               @lexijamesesq
/.house-qa.json                                 @lexijamesesq

# --- Governance & policy ---
/.claude/settings.json                          @lexijamesesq
/.github/CODEOWNERS                             @lexijamesesq

# --- Release / identity (plugin version = release identity; build config) ---
/.claude-plugin/marketplace.json                @lexijamesesq
/plugins/incubator/.claude-plugin/plugin.json   @lexijamesesq
/pyproject.toml                                 @lexijamesesq

# --- Trust boundary: Bash auto-run allow-list + live DB writes ---
/.claude/competitive-landscape-settings.json    @lexijamesesq
/scripts/research-db.py                         @lexijamesesq

# UNOWNED by default (flow without the operator): Ideas/**, Examples/**,
# Templates/**, reference/**, plugins/incubator/** skill / agent content,
# .claude/skills/**, .claude/agents/**, *.sample.*, README.md, LICENSE.
